<title>ITALY: Bank of Italy sets $4.0 bln repo tender for Friday.</title>
<headline>Bank of Italy sets $4.0 bln repo tender for Friday.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Italy said it called a three-month $4.0 billion repurchase tender for Friday for government securities to be resold on February 26, 1997.</p>
<p>At the previous comparable operation for $4.0 billion on November 21, the minimum accepted rate stood at 7.20 percent and the average rate at 7.21 percent.</p>
<p>The amount renews a similar repo which expires on November 26.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
